  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back everywhere I removed it. I couldn't run the tests, typecheck or `arch` to confirm, because the shell was blocked.\n\n**Why it failed:** `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`. That contract isn't in this repo, so my search for readers of the field missed it. My earlier claim that nothing reads `channel` was wrong.\n\n**What I restored:**\n- **Source:** the `Channel` type, the `Order` and `NewOrder` fields, the validation, the request parsing, and the `OrderPlaced` event field.\n- **Tests:** the `channel` values in the test data, the expected event, and the validation test.\n- **Docs:** the `createApp` example in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nMy `git checkout` was denied, so I did this by hand with edits. The source and test files showed as modified on disk since I last read them, though my edits applied cleanly. Please run `git diff` against `main` to check it matches the original, then run `npm test`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run arch`.\n\nIf `channel` really should go, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that, the field can be removed in a follow-up change.",
